 with retriesPerEntry budget spent, `_onRetryable` checks `attemptsOnEntry >= retriesPerEntry` → `_failOver` → records. But the intermediate failures (the ones that led to wait-outs) are not recorded into queue health. In roles mode, queueState is null so it doesn't matter. Queue mode (issue #418) — is this a real regression? Let's think: queue mode is used by the provider queue (`/model` queue feature?). The pre-existing behavior for a retryable error with `delay <= maxWait` also goes through `_sleepAndRetry` without `recordFailure` — so intermediate paid retries were never recorded in queue health either. Only the failover records. So the wait-out path behaves like a paid retry (not recording) — consistent with existing behavior for retries. Actually wait, but cooldown marking matters: previously on excessive wait with no fallback, `_failover` would mark the entry's cooldown (so a next call starts elsewhere or at least the entry is benched). Now, on wait-out exhaustion, the budget-spent path eventually calls `_failOver` → `_failover` marks cooldown. So cooldown still gets marked on exhaustion. OK.

